3.2 A Unified View on Existing UQ Setups
We now show that our agent UQ formulation cap-
tures various existing UQs as special cases.
Reduction to single-step LLM UQ.When t= 1
and the action space is restricted to responses, LLM
UQ can be cast as a special case
U(F≤T) =U(O 0) +U(A 1|O0)≥U(A 1|O0),
where O0andA1denote the given question and the
corresponding model answer, respectively. Most
current LLM UQ literature addresses only the con-
ditional answer uncertainty U(A 1|O0)(Malinin
and Gales, 2021; Fadeeva et al., 2023; Farquhar
et al., 2024). A few also consider the question
ambiguity U(O 0)(Hou et al., 2024; Tomov et al.,
2025) to reflect the reality of wild user query (Min
et al., 2020).
Reduction to multi-step reasoning UQ.When
the action space involves multi-step reasoning (e.g.,
chain-of-thought, Wei et al. (2022)), we have
