C Alternative Uncertainty Measures
Although we have mainly focused on the above
three information-theoretic uncertainty measures
throughout the paper, there are plenty of alterna-
tives one can consider depending on the problem
setups. In this section, we examine some possi-
ble alternative uncertainty measures,Rényi entropy,
Tsallis entropy, andinformational energy. These
sophisticated measures may be worth investigating
for the LLM agents’ inference interface, character-
ized by long-range interactions, evolving memory,
and the multifractal property.
